# Phase 95c Track E.1 — VFS throughput + IPC-cost measurement gate. Gated behind
# M3OS_VFS_THROUGHPUT_REGRESSION=1. Boots m3OS, runs the ramdisk
# `vfs-throughput-probe` binary (write 8 MiB + read back + verify, bracketed
# by /proc/blkstats device-block-op snapshots), and asserts verify=ok plus
# direction-specific ceilings anchored to the per-block regression it guards
# (n_bytes/4096 ~= 2048 for 8 MiB): write_calls_delta <= 3/4*per-block (1536),
# read_calls_delta <= 1/2*per-block (1024). Measured baseline write~=649 /
# read~=134 (write is metadata-dominated), so the ceilings clear the baseline yet
# trip on a collapse to per-block round-trips. Requires no special ports or host
# toolchain (the probe binary is always embedded in the ramdisk).
# Set this on branches touching vfs_server's ext2 read/write path, the VFS IPC
# caps (VFS_MAX_PREAD/PWRITE), the block-request coalescing, or the
# /proc/blkstats counters.
if [ "${M3OS_VFS_THROUGHPUT_REGRESSION:-0}" = "1" ]; then
